MemTile store-and-forward hop vs direct shim<->core transport, same bytes
=========================================================================

Machine   Desktop 2 (DESKTOP-CBL5NUA), AMD Ryzen 7 8700G (Phoenix NPU), Windows 11 Pro build 26200
Date      2026-09-16, sitting ended 15:23 UTC
Env       mlir-aie ironenv via scripts/research-iron.sh; host otherwise idle
Tool      tools/memtile_hop_probe.py (branch activation-residency)

Design    one core at (0,2); objects 6,400 B in and 3,200 B out (the engine's activation packet and output
          block); the core takes one input and produces one output per object with no compute. Transfers
          issued as shim_dma_single_bd_task by fifo name, one input task and one awaited output task.
Routes    dd  shim -> core,            core -> shim
          md  shim -> MemTile -> core, core -> shim            (ObjectFifo forward on tile (0,1))
          dm  shim -> core,            core -> MemTile -> shim
          mm  shim -> MemTile -> core, core -> MemTile -> shim
Volumes   512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192 objects = 3.3, 6.6, 13.1, 26.2, 52.4 MB in (outputs half)

Commands
  bash scripts/research-iron.sh tools/memtile_hop_probe.py build
  bash scripts/research-iron.sh tools/memtile_hop_probe.py sit --rounds 3 --iters 30 --json <json>
Every measurement ran in its own child process (3 warm-up + 30 timed dispatches); 3 rounds, order rotated
and reversed between rounds. Raw per-dispatch times: memtile_hop_phoenix_20260916T1523Z.json.
Smoke dispatches before the sitting: dd x512 mean 0.572 ms over 5; mm x8192 mean 7.760 ms over 5.

Mean dispatch ms (mean of the three round means)
  objects      512     1024     2048     4096     8192
  dd         0.584    1.047    1.994    3.878    7.609
  md         0.582    1.047    2.000    3.889    7.596
  dm         0.585    1.044    1.990    3.898    7.617
  mm         0.587    1.055    2.010    3.881    7.607

Least-squares fit over all 15 points per route: dispatch ms = intercept + slope * MB in
  dd  slope 0.14301 ms/MB  intercept 0.117 ms
  md  slope 0.14278 ms/MB  intercept 0.122 ms
  dm  slope 0.14327 ms/MB  intercept 0.116 ms
  mm  slope 0.14280 ms/MB  intercept 0.127 ms

  hop on the input path   md - dd                = -0.00023 ms per MB in
  hop on the output path  (dm - dd) * 2          = +0.00053 ms per MB out
  additivity              mm - dd = -0.00021;  (md - dd) + (dm - dd) = +0.00004 ms per MB in

Result: a MemTile store-and-forward hop costs nothing measurable per byte at the engine's object sizes.
The weight buffer's measured loss (0.044 ms per MB) would have been a 30% slope difference here.

Not run: the engine's actual split (one MemTile S2MM to four cores) and join shapes, several columns in
parallel, and object sizes other than 6,400 / 3,200 B. This sitting cannot say whether a column's rate is
set per byte or per object, because both scale together in every route.
